### switchbot-home backend — manual API requests
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the IntelliJ/JetBrains
### HTTP Client. Run `cargo run -p backend` first.

@host = http://localhost:3000

### List all devices (including blacklisted)
GET {{host}}/devices

### Latest reading for every non-blacklisted device
GET {{host}}/readings/latest


### --- Requests below need a real device_id ---
### Copy one from the "List all devices" response above (or from the
### `switchbot advertisement received` log lines with RUST_LOG=debug)
### and set it here.

@device_id = REPLACE_ME

### Latest reading for one device
GET {{host}}/devices/{{device_id}}/latest

### Historical readings for one device (defaults to the last 24h)
GET {{host}}/devices/{{device_id}}/readings

### Historical readings within an explicit range
GET {{host}}/devices/{{device_id}}/readings?from=2026-08-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-08-22T00:00:00Z

### Set a label and room
PUT {{host}}/devices/{{device_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Cucina",
  "room": "Cucina"
}

### Clear the label (send an empty string)
PUT {{host}}/devices/{{device_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": ""
}

### Blacklist a device (collector will stop storing its readings)
PUT {{host}}/devices/{{device_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blacklisted": true
}

### Un-blacklist it
PUT {{host}}/devices/{{device_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blacklisted": false
}

### Update on an unknown device_id returns 404
PUT {{host}}/devices/does-not-exist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "x"
}
